Preserve the original sub-pixel stroke width when subpixelStrokeWidth=false.

The upstream library clamps any stroke-width below 1 to 1 and tags the path
with vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke". That loses the original Flash twip
width — which our downstream renderer needs to apply the Flash-twip rule
`effective_width = max(width, 1 / resolution)`.

With this patch the vector-effect tag is still added (so the renderer still
recognizes the stroke as non-scaling), but the stored width stays at its
original float value (e.g. 0.05 for a Flash hairline).

--- a/src/Extractor/Drawer/Svg/SvgBuilder.php
+++ b/src/Extractor/Drawer/Svg/SvgBuilder.php
@@ -121,8 +121,12 @@
         if ($path->style->lineWidth > 0) {
             $width = $path->style->lineWidth / 20;

             if (!$this->subpixelStrokeWidth && $width < 1) {
-                $width = 1;
+                // Preserve the original sub-pixel width (Flash stores strokes in twips).
+                // The downstream renderer honors vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" with
+                // Flash-twip semantics: effective_width = max(width, 1 / resolution), so a
+                // hairline always renders as at least 1 screen pixel but grows when zoomed
+                // in enough that the stored width itself exceeds one screen pixel.
                 $pathElement->addAttribute('vector-effect', 'non-scaling-stroke');
             }

